language ESSENCE' 1.0
$ Five children at Hebrew school (Bernice, Carl, Debby, Sammy, Ted) each told one part of the Exodus story; each has an age (three, five, seven, eight, ten), and a family that came from one country (Ethiopia, Kazakhstan, Lithuania, Morocco, Yemen). Find the association of age, child, country and story.
letting AV = [3, 5, 7, 8, 10]
$ the value v of ages[a] is the bundle (age, child, country, story) of the bundle number v; the same number links the four lists
find ages : matrix indexed by [int(1..5)] of int(1..5)
find children : matrix indexed by [int(1..5)] of int(1..5)
find countries : matrix indexed by [int(1..5)] of int(1..5)
find stories : matrix indexed by [int(1..5)] of int(1..5)

branching on [children, countries, stories, ages]

such that
$ each age, child, country and story belongs to exactly one bundle
allDiff(ages),
allDiff(children),
allDiff(countries),
allDiff(stories),
$ Debby's family is from Lithuania (children 3 is Debby, countries 3 is Lithuania)
children[3] = countries[3],
$ the child who told the story of the Passover is two years older than Bernice (children 1)
forAll a, c : int(1..5) . ((ages[a] = stories[4] /\ ages[c] = children[1]) -> AV[a] = AV[c] + 2),
$ the child whose family is from Yemen (countries 5) is younger than the child from the Ethiopian family (countries 1)
forAll a, c : int(1..5) . ((ages[a] = countries[5] /\ ages[c] = countries[1]) -> AV[a] < AV[c]),
$ the child from the Moroccan family (countries 4) is three years older than Ted (children 5)
forAll a, c : int(1..5) . ((ages[a] = countries[4] /\ ages[c] = children[5]) -> AV[a] = AV[c] + 3),
$ Sammy (children 4) is three years older than the child who told the story of Moses's youth (stories 3)
forAll a, c : int(1..5) . ((ages[a] = children[4] /\ ages[c] = stories[3]) -> AV[a] = AV[c] + 3)
